The sources of LumenHEIF 1.0
============================

LumenHEIF is Lumen's HEIF plug-in. It is built from:

- lumenheif.c (in ffmpeg-patches): LumenHEIF itself, copyright (c) 2026
  Andrew Youll, MIT licence. Lumen's full source, including the EXIF code
  it uses (src/core/exif.c), is at https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-lumen
- libheif-1.23.7.tar.gz: libheif 1.23.7 as released (tag v1.23.7), GNU
  LGPL 3.
- ffmpeg-5.1.10.tar.xz: FFmpeg 5.1.10 as released, GNU LGPL 2.1 or later
  as built here (only the HEVC decoder and its parser; no GPL parts).
- ffmpeg-patches: the changes made to FFmpeg for RISC OS (from
  riscos-ffmpeg, plus 0101), the NEON alignment rewrite applied to its
  ARM assembly (neon-align.py: RISC OS stops unaligned loads), and
  build-heif.sh, the script that applies them and builds both libraries
  as LumenHEIF uses them.

To rebuild LumenHEIF with changed versions of the libraries, build them
with build-heif.sh (or your own way, with the same options), then link
lumenheif.c and exif.c against them, as Lumen's Makefile does (target
LumenHEIF,ff8).
